0..73 Comment "// The syntax\'s constructors and operations respect paths: the successor,"
74..151 Comment "// a variable, an abstraction, weakening and a substitution each carry a path"
152..223 Comment "// between their arguments to one between their results. `cong` takes a"
224..293 Comment "// named function, so each constructor is given one; a substitution\'s"
294..352 Comment "// congruence in its term is a `transport` along the path."
354..403 Comment "// The naturals; the syntax and its substitution."
